The machine needs two nexioms. If it only needed one, testing varogu, galopu and zanima would have lit up. Four pairs are still possible:
- {varogu, sodorer}
- {pulumin, galopu}
- {pulumin, sodorer}
- {galopu, sodorer}

Since the machine needs both nexioms on it, testing varogu, galopu and sodorer splits these evenly:
- **It lights** if the pair is {varogu, sodorer} or {galopu, sodorer}.
- **It stays dark** if the pair is {pulumin, galopu} or {pulumin, sodorer}.

Either way, two pairs will remain and I'll have to pick one of them.

TEST: varogu, galopu, sodorer
